# SwiftUI/MacOS: Contents Scrapping With AccessibilityAPI
## Hopefully it covers a lot….So that we can make a screen reader!
What do I want in this article? Some generic information on the active application! The tabs, the content!
The idea is pretty simple! We loop just like we would with HTML DOM! However, as we all know by now, the document for AccessibilityAPI is basically the same as not-existing!

## Basic Steps
1. Create a system-wide accessibility object with `[AXUIElementCreateSystemWide](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applicationservices/1462095-axuielementcreatesystemwide)` . In general, this `AXUIElement` will have two attributes available, `kAXFocusedUIElementAttribute` and `kAXFocusedApplicationAttribute` . I will be sharing with you two different approaches, traversing down from the `kAXFocusedApplicationAttribute` and up from `kAXFocusedUIElementAttribute` .
2. Call `[AXUIElementCopyAttributeValue](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applicationservices/1462085-axuielementcopyattributevalue)` on either `kAXFocusedUIElementAttribute` or `kAXFocusedApplicationAttribute` to get an `AXUIElement` .
3. Get the attributes available on the element using `AXUIElementCopyAttributeNames` (or `AXUIElementCopyParameterizedAttributeNames` for parameterized ones such as range, bounds, and etc.

